meta {
  name: config — bad key rejected BY THE FUNCTION
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{supabase_url}}/functions/v1/config?apiKey=pk_live_deliberately_invalid
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 401
  res.body.error: eq invalid_apiKey
}

docs {
  Also 401 — but a DIFFERENT 401, and the difference is the whole point.

  `{"error":"invalid_apiKey"}` is the function's own rejection after resolving the tenant. The
  gateway's refusal is `{"code":"UNAUTHORIZED_NO_AUTH_HEADER"}`. Identical status, opposite
  meanings: one says the stack is healthy and the key is wrong, the other says nothing ran.

  Asserting on the BODY rather than the status is what makes this test able to tell them apart —
  the lesson that cost a day of debugging.
}
